@dllehr-amd : Regarding our discussion and your recommendation to check whether the suggested changes affect CUDA detrimentally. **CUDA is affected, but nothing breaks.** `_output_projection` is platform-neutral so the NVIDIA path now runs `RMSNormGated` on a 3D (N, H, D) tensor too. Despite the [ROCm] tag, this is a change to shared model code. The 3D layout does not break any 2D fusion on the CUDA side, and CUDA actually gets the same win this PR claims for ROCm.

* Fusions: `MatcherRMSNormGated` is referenced only by `vllm/compilation/passes/fusion/rocm_aiter_fusion.py`.  The platform-neutral `RMSNormQuantFusionPass` only has non-gated patterns and none of them include the SiLU gate, so they could not have matched the GDN output norm before the change either.

* Output shape: `out_proj` still receives exactly the same 2D (N, H*D) tensor, because flatten(-2) on the 3D norm output produces it directly instead of via the removed reshape round trip.
